      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Prostoy Durak",
          "subtitle": "Simple Fool",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Prostoy Durak (Simple Fool) is a Durak variant with 5-card hands. Attacker plays 1, 3, or 5 cards (single; pair+1; two pairs+1 or four+1). Defender beats each or picks up. No throwing-in. 36 cards. Last with cards = Fool. Poland: DureÅ„ PiÄ…tkowy."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Prostoy durak (simple fool) is a Russian shedding game and a simpler relative of Podkidnoy Durak: it has no throwing-in by other players—only the attacker leads one, three, or five cards and the defender beats or picks up. It is now less widely played than Podkidnoy but remains familiar to many who learned it from their parents. The game is also played in Poland as Dureń Piątkowy (five-card fool)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Setup",
          "subtitle": "Table, deck, equipment, and deal",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "2-4. No partnerships."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "36 cards. Rank A-K-Q-J-10-9-8-7-6."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "36-card pack."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "5 each. One face-up for trump. Stock on top."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Variations",
          "subtitle": "Known ways this game changes",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "style": "unordered",
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Dureń Piątkowy Warsaw: Combines with Podkidnoy features."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
